cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Extensibly causal processes that are not purifiable (Open Quantum Problem 43): a Lean 4 formalization"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "David"
    family-names: "Turturean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of a negative answer to IQOQI Vienna Open Quantum Problem 43,
  "Are all extensibly causal processes purifiable?": an explicit process matrix for two parties
  with qubit inputs and outputs is extensibly causal and not purifiable (purity in the sense of
  Araújo, Feix, Navascués and Brukner). The development also proves that, for two parties
  with positive finite port dimensions, every extensibly causal process is purifiable
  exactly when the minimum port dimension is one.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal verification"
  - "process matrices"
  - "indefinite causal order"
  - "extensible causality"
  - "purification postulate"
  - "Open Quantum Problems"
